Record how this router may be reached over the network.

Until this is done the box serves its web UI and refuses everything
else over the network, so this is the step that makes it usable from
another machine. Normally it happens in the browser — the UI asks on
the first visit — and this exists for a box you only ever reach by SSH.

Use --password to read a password from redirected stdin, or
--no-password to allow anyone who can reach this box to configure it.
Passwords need at least 12 characters; do not put them in command arguments.

Claiming works once.

Usage:
  olr claim [flags]

Flags:
  -h, --help          help for claim
      --no-password   require no password; anyone on the network can configure this router
      --password      require a password read from redirected stdin

Global Flags:
      --dry-run         show what would change and exit without applying it
  -o, --output string   output format: text|json (default "text")
      --socket string   olrd control socket (default "/run/olr/olrd.sock")
